WEBVTT

00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:02.554
Last video ended on this curve: e to

00:00:02.574 --> 00:00:04.082
the x, over x plus one.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.988
At x equals minus one, the bottom is

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:09.574
zero, and you can't divide by zero, so

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:10.576
there's no curve there.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.367
Now the slope at x equals zero.

00:00:13.932 --> 00:00:15.945
A quick guess: divide the derivatives.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.290
The top's derivative is e to the x,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.852
and the bottom's is one, so the guess

00:00:20.893 --> 00:00:23.133
gives a slope of one at x equals

00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:23.514
zero.

00:00:24.096 --> 00:00:25.624
But the tangent there is flat.

00:00:26.328 --> 00:00:28.694
So how do we really differentiate a quotient,

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:30.579
and keep track of where it's defined?

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:32.722
Think about what each part does.

00:00:33.388 --> 00:00:34.693
For this positive fraction,

00:00:35.216 --> 00:00:38.328
top growth pushes up and bottom growth pulls

00:00:38.389 --> 00:00:38.669
down.

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:41.558
At x equals zero, the top, e to

00:00:41.599 --> 00:00:43.303
the x, is growing at a rate of

00:00:43.545 --> 00:00:45.951
one, and that pushes y up at a

00:00:45.992 --> 00:00:46.413
rate of one.

00:00:47.056 --> 00:00:49.724
The bottom, x plus one, is also growing

00:00:49.786 --> 00:00:51.370
at a rate of one, and that pulls

00:00:51.592 --> 00:00:52.996
y down at a rate of one.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.686
The push and the pull cancel, so the

00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:56.488
slope is zero.

00:00:57.252 --> 00:00:59.337
At x equals one, the push is about

00:00:59.498 --> 00:01:01.603
one point three six, and the pull is

00:01:01.624 --> 00:01:02.666
about point six eight,

00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:05.174
so the slope is about point six eight.

00:01:05.757 --> 00:01:07.883
That pull is the minus sign in the

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:08.445
quotient rule.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:10.698
You met the quotient rule in Year 11.

00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:12.758
Here's why it has that shape.

00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:15.771
Dividing by g is the same as multiplying

00:01:15.812 --> 00:01:18.401
by one over g, so use last video's

00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:19.024
product rule.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.974
The top's turn is f prime, times one

00:01:22.034 --> 00:01:22.415
over g.

00:01:23.097 --> 00:01:25.001
For the bottom's turn, the chain rule says

00:01:25.181 --> 00:01:28.047
one over g has derivative minus g prime,

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:28.908
over g squared.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:31.556
So that turn is minus f g prime,

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:32.359
over g squared.

00:01:33.163 --> 00:01:35.189
Put both turns over g squared, and you

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.578
get f prime g, minus f g prime,

00:01:38.061 --> 00:01:39.023
all over g squared.

00:01:39.787 --> 00:01:42.195
The top's derivative comes first, the minus is

00:01:42.216 --> 00:01:44.162
the bottom's pull, and the whole bottom is

00:01:44.223 --> 00:01:44.644
squared.

00:01:45.446 --> 00:01:46.447
Check our curve at zero:

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.171
f prime g is one,

00:01:48.713 --> 00:01:50.455
f g prime is one, so the top

00:01:50.556 --> 00:01:52.358
is one minus one, which is zero.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.043
Let's use it on our curve.

00:01:54.669 --> 00:01:58.156
Before differentiating, write where it's defined: x can't

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:58.918
be minus one.

00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:00.232
Now the parts.

00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:03.176
f is e to the x, and so

00:02:03.238 --> 00:02:03.861
is f prime.

00:02:04.405 --> 00:02:07.097
g is x plus one, so g prime

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:07.700
is one.

00:02:08.444 --> 00:02:10.307
The top of the answer is e to

00:02:10.328 --> 00:02:13.474
the x times x plus one, minus e

00:02:13.515 --> 00:02:14.596
to the x times one.

00:02:15.298 --> 00:02:16.801
Take out e to the x, and the

00:02:16.842 --> 00:02:19.827
bracket becomes x plus one minus one, which

00:02:19.908 --> 00:02:20.609
is just x.

00:02:21.312 --> 00:02:23.618
So d y by d x is x

00:02:23.819 --> 00:02:25.965
e to the x, over x plus one

00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:28.613
squared, for x not equal to minus one.

00:02:29.396 --> 00:02:31.963
At x equals zero, that's zero, the flat

00:02:32.044 --> 00:02:32.765
tangent we saw.

00:02:33.392 --> 00:02:34.204
Now a harder one.

00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:36.892
Differentiate y equals the natural log of x,

00:02:37.113 --> 00:02:39.457
over cos x, and find the gradient at

00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:40.259
x equals one.

00:02:41.204 --> 00:02:43.715
The outside operation is division, so it's the

00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:44.358
quotient rule.

00:02:45.102 --> 00:02:45.757
Domain first.

00:02:46.384 --> 00:02:48.768
The natural log needs x positive, and the

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:51.474
bottom can't be zero, so cos x can't

00:02:51.515 --> 00:02:51.955
be zero.

00:02:52.784 --> 00:02:53.330
Now the parts.

00:02:54.018 --> 00:02:55.747
f is the natural log of x, so

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.336
f prime is one over x.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.330
g is cos x, so g prime is

00:03:00.472 --> 00:03:01.396
minus sine x.

00:03:02.321 --> 00:03:04.350
f prime g is cos x over x.

00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:07.479
Then minus f g prime is minus the

00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:09.927
natural log of x, times minus sine x,

00:03:10.309 --> 00:03:11.893
and the two minus signs make a plus.

00:03:12.716 --> 00:03:14.522
All of that sits over cos squared x.

00:03:15.902 --> 00:03:17.899
Now put x equals one.

00:03:18.522 --> 00:03:20.848
The natural log of one is zero, so

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:22.553
the second term on top vanishes.

00:03:23.174 --> 00:03:24.940
That's the bottom's pull disappearing:

00:03:25.482 --> 00:03:27.268
when the top is zero, a change in

00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:29.015
the bottom can't move the fraction.

00:03:29.837 --> 00:03:32.889
What's left is cos one, over cos squared

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.038
one, which is one over cos one.

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:38.606
With x in radians, that's about one point

00:03:38.727 --> 00:03:39.367
eight five,

00:03:39.869 --> 00:03:41.912
and the tangent at the point one, zero

00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:42.413
agrees.

00:03:43.316 --> 00:03:45.543
Get the order backwards, and you'd get minus

00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:48.333
one point eight five, a falling tangent, but

00:03:48.354 --> 00:03:49.377
the curve is rising there.

00:03:50.141 --> 00:03:52.373
And in degrees you'd get about one, which

00:03:52.414 --> 00:03:52.936
is also wrong.

00:03:53.702 --> 00:03:55.316
One more habit, for simplifying.

00:03:56.082 --> 00:03:59.862
Differentiate y equals sine x, over x squared.

00:04:00.485 --> 00:04:02.613
The bottom can't be zero, so x can't

00:04:02.633 --> 00:04:02.994
be zero.

00:04:03.856 --> 00:04:06.721
The quotient rule gives x squared cos x,

00:04:07.242 --> 00:04:08.885
minus two x sine x,

00:04:09.386 --> 00:04:10.427
all over x to the four.

00:04:11.391 --> 00:04:13.217
Both terms on top share a factor of

00:04:13.418 --> 00:04:15.646
x, so take it out, and cancel it

00:04:15.707 --> 00:04:17.011
with one x from the bottom.

00:04:17.694 --> 00:04:20.183
That's allowed only because x isn't zero.

00:04:20.904 --> 00:04:23.869
So the answer is x cos x, minus

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:24.690
two sine x,

00:04:25.211 --> 00:04:26.053
over x cubed,

00:04:26.654 --> 00:04:28.657
and it still comes with x not equal

00:04:28.697 --> 00:04:29.078
to zero.

00:04:29.861 --> 00:04:32.011
Cancelling a factor never gives back a point

00:04:32.031 --> 00:04:33.678
the original function didn't have.

00:04:34.269 --> 00:04:35.784
Here's the classic way to remember it.

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:38.760
Low dee high, minus high dee low,

00:04:39.344 --> 00:04:40.227
over low squared.

00:04:41.072 --> 00:04:42.820
High is the top, and low is the

00:04:42.841 --> 00:04:43.081
bottom.

00:04:43.965 --> 00:04:46.008
Low dee high means the bottom times the

00:04:46.029 --> 00:04:47.131
derivative of the top,

00:04:47.713 --> 00:04:49.636
which is the same as f prime g.

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:53.145
Saying low first keeps the order right, and

00:04:53.166 --> 00:04:54.830
the minus is the bottom's pull.

00:04:55.532 --> 00:04:57.977
And unlike a product, the order matters here:

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.005
reversing the terms negates the derivative.

00:05:03.753 --> 00:05:04.140
Your turn.

00:05:04.909 --> 00:05:07.877
Differentiate y equals e to the x, over

00:05:08.119 --> 00:05:10.264
x plus two, and state any value of

00:05:10.386 --> 00:05:11.789
x that must be excluded.

00:05:12.432 --> 00:05:13.257
Pause here to answer.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:25.343
Domain first:

00:05:25.905 --> 00:05:27.250
x can't be minus two.

00:05:28.074 --> 00:05:29.686
f prime is e to the x, and

00:05:29.726 --> 00:05:30.694
g prime is one.

00:05:31.075 --> 00:05:32.716
So the top is e to the x

00:05:32.796 --> 00:05:35.138
times x plus two, minus e to the

00:05:35.358 --> 00:05:35.478
x,

00:05:36.119 --> 00:05:37.880
which factors to e to the x, times

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:38.761
x plus one.

00:05:39.481 --> 00:05:41.363
So d y by d x is e

00:05:41.383 --> 00:05:43.544
to the x times x plus one, over

00:05:43.664 --> 00:05:46.006
x plus two squared, for x not equal

00:05:46.026 --> 00:05:46.627
to minus two.

00:05:47.469 --> 00:05:48.873
Start with high dee low instead,

00:05:49.376 --> 00:05:50.499
and you negate the derivative.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:52.573
Last one.

00:05:53.299 --> 00:05:56.088
Find the gradient of the curve y equals

00:05:56.209 --> 00:05:58.275
the natural log of x, over x,

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.062
at x equals e.

00:06:00.933 --> 00:06:01.721
Pause here to answer.

00:06:12.455 --> 00:06:14.905
For positive x, f prime is one over

00:06:15.127 --> 00:06:15.247
x,

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:16.934
and g prime is one.

00:06:17.597 --> 00:06:19.838
The top is one over x times x,

00:06:20.299 --> 00:06:22.480
minus the natural log of x, so it's

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:24.322
one minus the natural log of x.

00:06:24.903 --> 00:06:27.208
So d y by d x is one

00:06:27.429 --> 00:06:29.152
minus the natural log of x, over x

00:06:29.194 --> 00:06:29.513
squared.

00:06:30.357 --> 00:06:32.686
At x equals e, the natural log of

00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:35.158
e is one, so the gradient is zero.

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:37.886
Dividing the derivatives would give one over e,

00:06:37.928 --> 00:06:39.612
but the tangent at e is flat.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.644
A quotient combines both turns, with the minus

00:06:44.724 --> 00:06:46.846
in the bottom's term, and keeps its domain.

00:06:47.832 --> 00:06:50.187
Next, we'll use the sign of a derivative.

00:06:50.989 --> 00:06:52.751
Here's the derivative of our first curve,

00:06:53.271 --> 00:06:55.333
x e to the x, over x plus

00:06:55.453 --> 00:06:56.034
one squared.

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:58.696
Where is it positive, where is it negative,

00:06:59.117 --> 00:07:01.600
and what happens at x equals minus one?

00:07:04.268 --> 00:07:05.070
Here are the key notes.

00:07:05.714 --> 00:07:07.441
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:07.503 --> 00:07:07.984
to copy them.
